      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_bbf06407",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: having_a_bad_day?; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a man giving a thumbs-up while text humorously suggests that having a bad day could mean being a Siamese twin attached to a gay brother who has a date and the twin is the only one with an ass. This joke relies on degrading and mocking LGBTQ+ individuals by implying that being gay is inherently linked to being 'less desirable' or 'unattractive' (the 'ass' part), and it uses a grotesque, dehumanizing metaphor (Siamese twin) to mock the person's situation. The intent is to provoke laughter through humiliation and ridicule of a marginalized group, which qualifies as hateful content under the provided toxicity categories. The humor is rooted in prejudice and targets the sexual orientation of the person described, making it a direct attack based on a protected characteristic.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2e5cdf41"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
