      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_12afe711",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Hateful",
      "description": "The meme depicts a man giving a thumbs-up while text humorously suggests that having a bad day could mean being a Siamese twin attached to a gay brother who has a date and the twin is the only one with an ass. This joke relies on degrading and mocking LGBTQ+ individuals by implying that being gay is inherently linked to being 'less desirable' or 'unattractive' (the 'ass' part), and it uses a grotesque, dehumanizing metaphor (Siamese twin) to mock the person's situation. The intent is to provoke laughter through humiliation and ridicule of a marginalized group, which qualifies as hateful content under the provided toxicity categories. The humor is rooted in prejudice and targets the sexual orientation of the person described, making it a direct attack based on a protected characteristic.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2e5cdf41"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4af4c8a9",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "intended audience",
      "description": "The meme is designed for a general online audience familiar with internet humor, particularly those who appreciate or are exposed to hateful, degrading, and mocking humor that targets marginalized groups. The target community includes individuals who may find offensive stereotypes and prejudiced content amusing, often without realizing the harm caused. The humor relies on the audience's understanding of LGBTQ+ discrimination tropes, ableism, and body-shaming, suggesting the meme is intended for viewers who either do not recognize the offensive nature of the content or who are deliberately seeking out such material for shock value or dark comedy.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
